cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  OpenCompMech: verification-first generation of 2D compliant mechanisms
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - name: OpenCompMech Contributors
repository-code: "https://github.com/drozdja/opencompmech"
abstract: >-
  Research code for generating 2D compliant mechanisms across five generator
  families and verifying them with sparse finite-element analysis. A candidate
  counts only if a fresh FEA solve confirms it works, so results are reported as
  verified pass rates rather than similarity to a reference design. Includes a
  reusable, generator-independent SE(2)-equivariant graph representation with an
  ETNN-style combinatorial-complex lift, and a frozen evaluation protocol for
  comparing generative models under identical conditions.
keywords:
  - topology optimization
  - compliant mechanisms
  - finite element analysis
  - generative models
  - graph neural networks
  - equivariance
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
